- op: discuss  # a9e8
  at: '2026-11-17T15:46:33Z'  # a9e8
  by: agent  # a9e8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a9e8
  clock: 4  # a9e8
  nonce: a9e8  # a9e8
  message: "Merged in PR #2231 (dev 268e9cfda). THE OWNER'S CHECK, RUN FIRST (decision 16a): commit 5a38b95bb analysed by the installed build (dfca1edd8196f6bb, hypergumbo 10.0.0) and by the tree's own build (7821bf3427cc95d2), 69,013 nodes and 275,454 edges each; for each of 2,600 files alone and the 18 logged changed_source sets both graphs name the same test files: 2,618 same, 0 differ. Control: 2,000 edges deleted from one graph -> 174 sets differ. worktree/cross_build_out2.txt, cross_build_control.txt, cross_build_compare.py. ONE commit and ONE pair of builds, 17 pull requests apart: it does not say two builds further apart agree. WHAT WAS WRONG, which the description had as 'its own cache and its own analyzer identity': a worktree run pins PYTHONPATH to its sources, the installed hypergumbo inherited it and imported the worktree's code (identity dfca1edd8196f6bb without PYTHONPATH, 01971965111c44e4 with a tree's sources pinned), so the 'stable' slice was made by the code under test and no stored graph ever matched. BUILT: smart-test runs the installed hypergumbo with PYTHONPATH empty for the build name, the --minimal probe and the slice; graph-rebuild drops it for the analysis. No graph of ANOTHER build is ever used: a worktree now simply has the installed build, like the main checkout. CLOSE CONDITION: (1) the cross-build counts, above. (2) A LIVE worktree run (git worktree at ~/hg_wt/kitin_probe, PYTHONPATH pinned to its packages/*/src, its own XDG_CACHE_HOME, one source edit): 'selecting from stored graph 4 of 5a38b95bb, 1 commit(s) old: 12 seed file(s), 0 of them not this change's, reaching 0 test file(s) this change does not', wall 50 s; its own rebuild said 'the graph of 5a38b95bb is stored already (graph 4)'. worktree/live_worktree.txt. The probe worktree is removed. (3) Tests: test_the_installed_hypergumbo_never_inherits_the_runs_pythonpath and the rebuild's; mutations X2, X4, X5, X6 red. ALSO IN THIS PR: two stores at once (its own invariant item). CHANGED FOR ANYONE WHO SLICED WITH A TREE'S CODE ON PURPOSE: PYTHONPATH no longer reaches the installed command; a HOME whose .local/bin/hypergumbo is a wrapper that sets PYTHONPATH itself still does it (playbook)."  # a9e8
